cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the thesis."
abstract: "Code, data and results for a master's thesis that evaluates online changepoint methods (CUSUM, EWMA, FOCuS, FOCuS-AR, CPM and capped detectors, with PELT, Binary Segmentation and WBS as offline benchmarks) on daily NSW Opal train tap-ons and NSW electricity demand. Each detector runs on the forecast error of a past-only forecast of a normal day (same-weekday difference, median of four, Holt-Winters, yearly memory), with thresholds calibrated by simulation for a 5% chance of a false alarm in a year, allowing for autocorrelation. Includes the live electricity monitor at https://varuntree.github.io/nsw-normal-day-monitor/."
keywords:
  - changepoint detection
  - online monitoring
  - CUSUM
  - EWMA
  - FOCuS
  - Opal
  - electricity demand
title: "Detecting Real Changes in Daily Public Data Streams: Evaluating Online Changepoint Methods on NSW Opal Train Travel and Electricity Demand"
